  "query_preview": "as heat index values are forecasted to peak in the 105-110 \ndegree range across much of the area through the Labor Day Weekend. \nLate afternoon/early evening showers and storms should help keep \nparts of our CWA under Heat Advisory criteria. With the deep \ntropical moisture in place, some of these storms will have the \ncapability to produce locally heavy downpours at times. Regardless, \nan areawide Heat Advisory has been issued for Friday. As we go \nbeyond Friday, additional heat advisories will eventually be needed \nfor Saturday and Sunday. Heat trends will continue to be monitored \nas we go through the weekend. \n\nDangerous heat will continue to persist across the area as we head \ninto the new work week. Additional heat headlines/advisories will \neventually be needed as we get closer. Heat trends will begin to \ndecrease across parts of the area by the mid week as global guidance \nshows a frontal boundary pushing south across the area. Rain chances \nwill be possible mainly for areas along and south of I-20 heading \ninto Thursday. /CR/",
